 r←Test_Misc_014(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempFolder;filename;res;config1;config2;subFolder;filename2
⍝ Exercise Remove_githubUsername, including a sub-folder: the function walks the whole tree, and it
⍝ used to recurse into `RenameInfo_url_` rather than into itself, so nothing below the top folder was
⍝ ever cleaned. The sub-folder's config also carries `info_url`, which made that wrong call throw a
⍝ VALUE ERROR on `report`, a name that exists only in `RenameInfo_url`'s own scope.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 tempFolder←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI
 filename←tempFolder,'/cider.config'
 filename ⎕NCOPY⍠('IfExists' 'Replace')⊣##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/cider.config.GitHubUserName'

 subFolder←tempFolder,'/sub'
 'Create!'FilesAndDirs.CheckPath subFolder
 filename2←subFolder,'/cider.config'
 filename2 ⎕NCOPY⍠('IfExists' 'Replace')⊣##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/cider.config.GitHubUserName'
 config2←##.Cider.Get_JSON5 filename2
 config2.CIDER.info_url←'https://example.com'
 {}config2 ##.Cider.WriteProjectConfig filename2

 config1←##.Cider.ReadProjectConfig filename
 Assert'JohnDoe'≡config1.CIDER.githubUsername

 res←##.Cider.Remove_githubUsername tempFolder
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠≢res                                                   ⍝ Both files must be reported
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠(##.Cider.Get_JSON5 filename).CIDER.⎕NC'githubUsername'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠(##.Cider.Get_JSON5 filename2).CIDER.⎕NC'githubUsername'
⍝ `info_url` is none of this function's business and must be left where it is
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=(##.Cider.Get_JSON5 filename2).CIDER.⎕NC'info_url'

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 FilesAndDirs.RmDir tempFolder,'/..'
 ⍝Done
